\newlabel{fig:snapshot}{{3}{2}{Layout of one snapshot, $16 + 12N$ bytes (52 bytes for 3 players, 3\,616 for 300). The ENet server writes it into one byte array and sends it as a remote procedure call; the C++ server sends the same bytes directly in UDP datagrams of at most 1\,200 bytes.\relax }{figure.caption.3}{}}
